I think you have an old terra version, since there was a bug in that package for numerical layer indexing. It was fixed a while ago; see the terra changelog on cran.

Upgrade terra and also inlabru, to 2.14.1, since there have been changes and bug fixes in inlabru as well.

But it shouldnt need to call the fill_missing code at all, if your covariate covers your samplers (also make sure to use the full argument name samplers instead of the shortened sampler).

Finn Lindgren
email: finn.l...@gmail.com

