Even if you use common parameters, the resolutions don't necessarily need to be the same; you just need the largest triangles within the domain(s) of interest to be smaller than the correlation range, so that the "worst" triangle resolution is fine enough.
The resolution difference should mostly matter if you have too coarse resolution in some areas but not others.

Finn

